readonly-wrapped float64 is mis-handled on the ILP32 VM: is64BitScalar / lowerCast / LOAD_IMM peel only TYP_NAMED (vmUnwrapNamed), not TYP_READONLY, so a `readonly float64` is mis-sized to one slot and mis-classified as non-float — its value truncates to the low word (e.g. 50.0 -> 0.0).  readonly int64 is unaffected.  A `readonly float64` capture therefore reads back 0.  Fix: strip all wrappers (types.StripWrappers) at every VM float-vs-int / 64-bit-scalar classification site.  See claude-todo.md.
